ms vs 0.3 ms on the default menu (single-machine timings, noisy). QV4 interprets or JITs differently, and no test measures it there. The PR body now states that Quickshell's FileView already drops a BOM at the very start of the file; no in-scope test records that, and a BOM later in the file still reaches the parser. The baseline's new menu-live suite runs menu-acceptance-test.sh in quickshell with a user JSONC that has trailing commas and commas inside strings (menu-acceptance-test.sh:172), but the package links it to no parser requirement, so its outcome is not evidence here, and it feeds no BOM, Unicode space or inline comment and measures no parse time.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":1045},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":1056},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js","kind":"file","line":39},{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-acceptance-test.sh","kind":"file","line":172},{"id":"SW-REQ-261001-BNZG","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"medium","title":"Question: does the scanner behave and perform the same under Quickshell's QV4 engine as under node?","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"QV4 witness: parse the default menu and a BOM/NBSP user extension inside Quickshell\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"claim":{"params":{"relatesTo":["shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js:parseMenuJsonc","SW-REQ-260922-7NPE"],"scenario":"upgrade with an existing ~/.config/omarchy/extensions/omarchy-menu.jsonc that has an inline // comment and overrides a shipped id: base shows 0 user rows and the shipped row; does head replace the shipped row with the user override?"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"A user file with an inline // comment, or a Unicode space or BOM between tokens, used to contribute 0 rows; the shipped menu kept working. After this PR the same file parses, and its ids override shipped ones per SW-REQ-260922-7NPE. That is the PR's purpose, but an upgrade can change a user's menu without any edit on their part (e.g. an old, forgotten override now becomes active).","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":1056},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-7NPE","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260928-C8W1","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"low","title":"Question: do user extensions that silently loaded as empty before now load and override shipped entries after upgrade?","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Upgrade witness: inline-commented user extension overriding a shipped id\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"detail":"I ran both: a CR-only file with a // comment (`// c\\r{...}`) and a /* */ block comment give 0 rows at base and at head. The scanner ends a comment only at \\n and has no block-comment state. The PR's docs/menu.md now says block comments are not supported. These KIs pre-date the PR.","refs":[{"id":"proof/known-issues/KI-MENU-JSONC-CR-LINE-ENDINGS.yaml","kind":"file","line":1},{"id":"proof/known-issues/KI-MENU-JSONC-STRIP-GAPS.yaml","kind":"file","line":1},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-E4J2","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"info","title":"KI-MENU-JSONC-CR-LINE-ENDINGS and KI-MENU-JSONC-STRIP-GAPS remain open; the PR does not change them","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"detail":"effects_unavailable: review.effects covers C/C++ only, so callers, gained effects, new mutable state and call-level requirement impact are not in the package for this JS change. The scope approximations say no uncodified connection could be detected, so 'No spec-gap candidates' proves nothing here. By reading: stripJsonc/parseMenuJsonc add no callees, no I/O, and no state beyond local variables.","refs":[{"id":"review.effects.approximations","kind":"check"},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js","kind":"file","line":2}],"severity":"info","title":"Change effects not analyzed; scope analysis bounds acknowledged","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"detail":"Each of the 135 compat_change_unapproved disclosures prevents readiness until a reviewer or above approves it under the approved policy @ 39746e65, or the author fixes it. The next decision states the exact count (\"Approve each of the 135 backward-compatibility changes\"). My reading that each difference is intended is commentary, not an approval.","refs":[{"id":"review.compat","kind":"check"}],"severity":"info","title":"All 135 compatibility findings stay unapproved; only a human reviewer can approve them","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}}],"packageDigest":"sha256:8329011ffe3c5f7ec50029fe8cc819801ccb4f470d99cb6c17bdd301b86e950f","packageIdentity":"epkg-c7bc47edc8005bced3aad1d60bcf6407f2fc756cdd5db48e379bf1a5cf9e1b70","riskAssessment":{"level":"medium","rationale":"Small parser change. Each fix has differential and observed test evidence, all 127 differences match a requirement, and the fuzz found nothing worse than the base. But 135 compatibility changes are unapproved (prevents ready), the production QV4 runtime and its parse cost are untested, and upgraded users' previously-ignored extension files will start to apply."},"schemaVersion":"reqproof.review-annotation.v1","suggestedTests":[{"forClaim":30,"rationale":"Settles whether production QV4 matches node on /\\s/, BOM delivery via FileView.text(), and parse latency.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":1045},{"id":"SW-REQ-261001-BNZG","kind":"requirement"}],"title":"QV4 witness: parse the default menu and a BOM/NBSP user extension inside Quickshell"},{"forClaim":31,"rationale":"Shows base (override ignored) vs head (override active), so the release note can warn users.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":1056},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-7NPE","kind":"requirement"}],"title":"Upgrade witness: inline-commented user extension overriding a shipped id"}],"summary":"**What the PR does.** Upstream #13968 (buger; ff77cd02 + b2dae8db, the live head) replaces stripJsonc's two regexes with one string-aware scanner and makes parseMenuJsonc return no rows for an array root. It fixes #13250 (a comma before } or ] inside a string was eaten), #13492 (an array root became rows \"0\",\"1\") and #13493 (an inline // emptied the file). b2dae8db also reads every JS whitespace character outside strings (BOM, NBSP, U+2000-200A, U+2028/9, U+3000, VT, FF) as a space. Mirror commit 499d81b8 applies it onto baseline quattro-proof 39746e65; the 14 later commits are our proof work. Advisory audit; not an approval.\n\n**Is the fix verified?** Changed code is fully covered: 17/17 decision lines, 34/34 decisions. Test results are current, 56/56 passed (run-caa25a7c). All obligation cells of the 6 parser requirements are observed_pass. I ran base 39746e65 and head: each issue reproduces at base and is fixed at head; 200k fuzzed inputs: none worse.\n\n**Compatibility.** Readiness is not_assessed. Next decision: human_judgement (compat_changes_unapproved), \"Approve each of the 135 backward-compatibility changes\", by a reviewer under the approved policy @ 39746e65. 135 compat_change_unapproved disclosures prevent readiness. I checked all 127 differences: 123 data inputs with a JS whitespace character go from parse error to parsed (BNZG); 4 are the issue reproducers. The 5 test_diff findings are tests renamed and flipped from expected failure to fixed. The 3 unapproved removed_behavior findings are intended too. Only a human can approve them.\n\n**Questions for a human.** (1) Does Quickshell's QV4 engine match node on /\\s/ and on cost (in node stripJsonc is ~4x slower on the default menu, ~16x on 1.1 MB)? No test runs it in QV4. (2) User extension files that loaded empty before (inline comment, Unicode space) now load and can override shipped entries after an upgrade.\n\n**Traceability.** stripJsonc and parseMenuJsonc are traced at function level: E4J2, 3T3F, 66FW, C8W1, BNZG, BMFE (4 added; 3 modified, with PPDW). 23 more requirements are code_changed only via file-level test traces; their 27 not_linked cells have no tagged test. No spec-gap candidates; change effects were not analyzed (effects_unavailable).\n\n**Not caused by this PR.** KI-MENU-JSONC-CR-LINE-ENDINGS and -STRIP-GAPS stay open (the PR does not change them). The baseline's move to medium for KI-MENU-OPEN-LEAVES-CONFIRM is unrelated; the PR does not touch it. No gate fails; 13 checks were skipped."}
